  "title": "Preguntó Si --- A Question That Stops Being One",
  "drivablePrefix": 1,
  "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:31555c0e2d959fc1",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "ES-C57-pregunto-si",
      "sequence": 2305,
      "title": "preguntó si",
      "headword": "preguntó si",
      "romanization": "preguntó si",
      "gloss": "he asked whether — reporting a question, which stops being a question the moment you report it",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:f74100b5d63a54de",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Report a statement. (Dijo que trabajaba.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now the past of preguntar, which is perfectly ordinary. (Preguntó.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: a question, reported",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "¿Trabaja? — the question, as asked. Preguntó si trabajaba. — the question, reported."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two things changed, and both are worth naming."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The joint is si, not que. A statement goes in on que; a yes-or-no question goes in on si. The verb still steps back into the imperfect, exactly as before — that part has not changed at all."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "culture-pragmatics",
          "title": "Why it's said this way",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And the question marks are gone. Not forgotten — not allowed. Look at what the reported sentence actually does: it tells you something. It is a statement about an act of asking, and nobody is being asked anything. The marks belong to a question being put, and no question is being put here."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So ¿Preguntó si trabajaba? is a real sentence, but it means something else — it asks whether he asked."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now the si itself. It is the same si that opens a condition, and that is not a coincidence dressed up as one. Both uses hold something open that has not been settled: si tengo tiempo leaves the time unsettled, si trabajaba leaves the answer unsettled. English splits the job between whether and if. Spanish never needed to."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "Preguntó si trabajaba",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
